  "challenge": {
    "title": "Meeting Family Over a Meal",
    "instructions": "Write and say a short Egyptian conversation of at least 10 lines. It must ask about someone's family, name at least one relative, say you are hungry or thirsty, order food or a drink, use the fixed exchange بالهنا والشفا / الله يعافيك, and ask for the bill. Use at least 8 target phrases from Unit 2 and address both a man and a woman.",
    "required_elements": [
      "A question about family using كام فرد في عيلتك؟ or عندك إخوات؟",
      "A relative named with أمي, أبويا, أخويا, أختي, جوزي, مراتي, ابني or بنتي.",
      "A statement of hunger or thirst using جعان, جعانة or عطشان.",
      "An order using عايز آكل or عايز أشرب.",
      "The fixed exchange بالهنا والشفا / الله يعافيك.",
      "A request for the bill using الحساب لو سمحت or الحساب كام؟",
      "Both a masculine form (إنت متجوز؟) and a feminine form (إنتي متجوزة؟)."
    ],
